title: DevShell Environment Implementation
status: proposed
created: 2026-11-07
author: adrian
context: "`adrs/2026-11-07-devshell-environment` specifies the `devshell` kind as a prototype and ships no production type. Its findings, and the six decisions recorded in `maps/2026-10-31-nix-devshell-sandbox` as T-027 to T-032, settle the shape this ADR implements. Kinds move out of the contract into a compiled-in registry, so a step is an identity, a kind name and the settings that kind owns, and the backend receives contributions rather than a kind. A backend reports static support for contribution sorts, which today are an environment and read-only mounts. The environment is captured by evaluating the `print-dev-env` script once in a sanitised shell and restoring the six variables nix-direnv restores. That keeps the exported-but-empty build-phase variables and never carries HOME, PWD, OLDPWD, SHLVL, `_` or the caller's temporary paths. A backend persists whatever it needs in its own `SandboxRecord.data` payload. Provenance keeps the kind as a string. The current contract cannot express any of this. `ProvisionKind` and `ProvisionStep` are closed enums at `crates/agentkit-litterbox/src/sandbox/contract.rs:74,117`. `Backend::provision_support` reports per kind at `contract.rs:98,489`. `CreateRequest` carries `provision: Vec<ProvisionStep>` and no contributions at `contract.rs:145-153`. The resolver refuses a kind the backend does not report at `crates/agentkit-litterbox/src/provision/resolve.rs:204-260`. The doctor prints a `ProvisionKind` at `crates/agentkit-litterbox/src/cli.rs:479`. Consent covers only `ProvisionStep::Command` at `crates/agentkit-litterbox/src/orchestrator/service.rs:542-560`. Docker reports only the command kind at `crates/agentkit-litterbox/src/backends/docker/backend.rs:720-728`. Terminology is normative in `crates/agentkit-litterbox/CONTEXT.md`, upstream Nix terms are in `.agentkit/tackle/prompts/nix/glossary.md`, and the behaviours this specification relies on are verified in `.agentkit/tackle/prompts/nix/PROMPT.md`."
problem: "A project cannot use the `devshell` kind that the prototype proved. The contract has a closed kind enum, support is reported per kind, the create request carries no contributions, the doctor is typed to the closed kind, consent covers only command steps, and no backend can receive or persist a host-prepared environment and store view. A project that declares the kind is rejected before anything is prepared."
goals[9]:
  - "Replace the closed kind enum with a compiled-in registry outside the contract, so a step is identity, kind and kind-owned settings."
  - "Add the production `devshell` kind: host requirements, environment capture, closure derivation and contributions."
  - "Carry contributions on the create request in step order and have a backend declare static support for each contribution sort."
  - "Persist contributions through the backend's own record payload so every later process sees the same environment and mounts."
  - "Report the kind, its host requirements, the installable, the closure count and the store view in the doctor, and report the same provenance in inspection."
  - "Consent-gate host evaluation exactly as command steps are gated."
  - "Keep nix outside the sandbox, refuse rather than realise, carry no shell state and fail closed."
  - "Keep Docker and every project without a devshell step behaving as they do today."
  - "Test the registry, the contribution model and the capture with unit and host tests, and document the configuration."
nonGoals[12]:
  - "Binding the contributed mounts in a backend; linux-bwrap-provider and darwin-sandbox-provider render them."
  - "The egress proxy (egress-proxy) and automatic backend selection (automatic-backend-selection)."
  - "Realising the devShell; the user runs nix develop on the host first."
  - "Dynamic discovery, a plugin path or runtime loading of kinds; the registry is a compiled-in table."
  - "Shell state in the sandbox: bash functions, aliases, shell options and the hook are not carried."
  - "Any contribution beyond an environment and read-only mounts added for symmetry."
  - "Migrating projects that hand-write environment variables to a devshell step."
  - "Changing MCP tool names or arguments."
  - "Shipping or referring to the prototype under adrs/2026-11-07-devshell-environment/poc."
  - "Caching a prepared devShell across creates; it is derived from the store on each create."
  - "A Nix backend; a devShell is an environment, not a mechanism."
  - "Implementing host-step contributions in Docker; Docker keeps reporting them unsupported."
requirements[21]{id,title,slug,description}:
  FR-001,"Kind: Compiled-In Registry",kind-registry,"The contract stops naming kinds. `ProvisionKind` and the closed `ProvisionStep` enum are removed from `crates/agentkit-litterbox/src/sandbox/contract.rs`. A provisioning step is an identity, a kind name and the settings that kind owns. A compiled-in registry under `src/provision/kind/` validates the settings, and each kind's host preparation is a separate module reached only by the orchestrator. The registry is a table, not discovery or a plugin path: adding a kind is one module and one entry. An unknown kind fails at configuration load, naming the identity and the kind. The contract carries the generic step and no kind-specific type."
  FR-002,"Kind: DevShell Step",devshell-step,"The registry contains two kinds: `command`, which runs inside the sandbox, and `devshell`, which runs on the host and changes what the sandbox sees. A `devshell` step carries `installable` and no other setting. Settings are validated at load: an unknown key, a missing installable or a second `devshell` step in one backend's sequence fails as Misconfigured, naming the identity and the conflicting identity when there is one."
  FR-003,"Core: Contributions",contributions,"A host step returns contributions: an environment, which is a map of variable name to value, and a list of absolute read-only mount paths, in step order. The contract defines those two sorts and names no devShell, flake, nix, store or mechanism. A backend applies them to every command in the sandbox. The vocabulary grows by amendment when a kind needs a new sort; it is not a fixed enumeration a kind has to fit into."
  FR-004,"Core: Contribution Support",contribution-support,"`Backend` replaces `provision_support` with a static `contribution_support` report. Each entry names a contribution sort, a state, a reason, a remedy and an optional fallback. Readiness stays in `Backend::readiness` and remains dynamic and host-specific. The resolver refuses a step whose contribution sort the selected backend does not report, before create, naming the step, the backend, the sort, the reason and the remedy. A backend never reports support per kind."
  FR-005,"Core: Request Contributions",request-contributions,"`CreateRequest` carries the resolved steps and their contributions. A step that runs on the host carries the environment and mounts it produced; a `command` step carries none. The backend applies the contributions in step order. A backend whose sequence does not name a step receives none of its contributions. A command step before the `devshell` step sees the default environment; one after it sees the prepared environment."
  FR-006,"Host: Requirements",host-requirements,"The `devshell` kind declares host requirements and checks them without mutating anything: nix is on PATH and reports a version, flakes are enabled, the installable evaluates, and the devShell is valid in the store. Each check returns a structured result with the primitive, the reason and a remedy the user can run. The doctor and create use one implementation, and neither prepares the devShell when a requirement is absent."
  FR-007,"Host: No Realisation",no-realisation,"The validity check is a store query, not a build. An unbuilt devShell is Unavailable, naming the installable and the remedy of running `nix develop <installable>` on the host. Litterbox creates no output path. `print-dev-env` may still copy a dirty flake source to the store and may build a source derivation; that is a store write, not a realisation, and the report says so rather than claiming nothing was written."
  FR-008,"Step: Environment Capture",environment-capture,"The environment is produced by evaluating the `print-dev-env` script once in a sanitised bash, with only HOME and a minimal PATH supplied, so the shell hook runs once. Records are read from a file or a spare descriptor, never from stdout where the hook can corrupt them. The contribution is the difference against the caller, with `NIX_BUILD_TOP`, `TMP`, `TMPDIR`, `TEMP`, `TEMPDIR` and `terminfo` restored to their caller values or unset. The capture starts from a caller that already has HOME, PWD, OLDPWD, SHLVL and `_`, so they are unchanged and never contributed. Exported-but-empty build-phase variables are contributed with their empty values."
  FR-009,"Core: No Shell State",no-shell-state,"Nothing that exists only inside a shell crosses into the sandbox: bash functions, aliases, shell options and the hook itself are not carried. The hook runs once on the host. A command that needs a shell function fails as it would in a plain shell, and no file is written to make it appear. The doctor says the sandbox carries no shell state."
  FR-010,"Step: Store Closure",store-closure,"The step derives the devShell's store closure with a host query over the output path that `print-dev-env` reports. Paths are de-duplicated and absolute, and each becomes one read-only mount. The closure is the default view; a machine setting selects the whole store instead. The contract sets no path limit. A backend that cannot mount the set validates it against its own limit and refuses before create with that limit, the contribution, the reason and the remedy."
  FR-011,"Core: Persistence",persistence,"The backend writes whatever it needs into its own `SandboxRecord.data` payload at create and reads it in `exec`, `inspect` and `delete`. The contract requires that every later command in every process sees the same environment and mounts, and that `inspect` reports provenance; it defines no payload shape. A prepared environment is derived at create. A later change to the flake or the host does not reach a running sandbox, and creating again prepares again. Delete removes the contributions with the record."
  FR-012,"Core: Provenance",provenance,"`StepProvenance` carries the step identity, the kind name as a string and one entry per variable the step changed, with the change kind. It never carries a value. `Provenance` carries the origin, the variables, the host paths that were reported rather than granted, and the steps that ran. `Inspection` exposes it unchanged. A variable that names a host path outside the store and the workspace is reported as a host path."
  FR-013,"Core: Workspace Mapping",workspace-mapping,"The step records which environment values name the project root, such as `CARGO_HOME`, `RUSTUP_HOME` and the leading PATH entry. When a backend presents the workspace at a path other than the host's, it rewrites only those values. Store paths, including the `NIX_` variables and toolchain paths, are never rewritten, because the store is mounted at its own path."
  FR-014,"Step: Host Placement",host-placement,"The `devshell` step runs during create, after resolution, contribution-support and consent checks and before the branch is created. It reads the project root, not the staged workspace, because the installable is relative to the checkout the user is in. It produces contributions and runs no sandbox. A failure leaves no branch, workspace or compute."
  FR-015,"Config: Consent",consent,"Preparing a devShell evaluates project code and runs its hook on the host, so it is consent-gated exactly as a command step is: the project's namespace is in `allowed-projects`, or `allow-project-setup` permits every project. A refusal is Denied, names the step identity and both settings, and no nix process starts. Cloning a repository is never consent to evaluate its flake."
  FR-016,"CLI: Doctor",doctor,"`litterbox doctor` reports, without creating or mutating anything: the selected backend and its readiness; the contribution sorts it supports; each step with its identity, kind, state, reason and remedy; the host requirements and whether each holds; the installable, whether it is valid in the store, the closure's path count and the store view in force. It creates no sandbox, workspace, branch or store path, and it never prepares a devShell. It exits non-zero when a required step is unavailable or denied."
  FR-017,"Core: Failure Classes",failure-classes,"A missing nix, disabled flakes, an installable that does not evaluate or a devShell that is not valid in the store is Unavailable, each with the primitive, the reason and a remedy. An installable that evaluates to something without a devShell environment is Misconfigured. A hook that exits non-zero is Failed, with the identity and bounded output. A backend that cannot meet a requirement or apply a contribution is Unsupported. A refused step is Denied. These are the existing provisioning classes."
  FR-018,"Core: No Nix Inside",no-nix-inside,"The contributions give the sandbox no route to nix: no daemon socket, no store write and no network. The devShell closure contains no nix executable, verified in this repository. A nix binary found elsewhere cannot reach the daemon because the socket is not contributed and the network is unshared. A command that expects to evaluate or build fails as it would on a host without nix, and the remedy is to run nix on the host and create again."
  FR-019,"Backend: Docker Compatibility",docker-compatibility,"The Docker backend reports no contribution sorts, because it does not apply a host step's environment or bind host paths for a step. A project whose sequence names a `devshell` step is refused as Unsupported before the container is created, naming the backend, the step and the first contribution it cannot apply. Command steps, the Docker record payload, exec and inspect are unchanged."
  FR-020,"Config: Compatibility",config-compatibility,"A project with no `devshell` step behaves exactly as it does today. The shapes of `[project] backends`, `[[provision]]` and `[backends.<name>].provision` do not change. An unknown kind still fails at load, and a known kind with an unknown setting still fails at load. The `setup-command` migration and its message do not change. MCP tool names and arguments do not change."
  FR-021,"Config: Store View",store-view-setting,"The store view is a machine-owned setting, either `closure` or `whole`, with `closure` as the default. It lives in the local override, not the project file, because it describes what the host can bind rather than what the project needs. The doctor reports the view in force and the path count it produces."
nonFunctional[9]{id,title,slug,description}:
  NFR-001,"Shared: No New Dependency",no-new-dependency,"The kind spawns nix and reads its output with the standard library and the `serde_json` already in the tree. It adds no crate, no async runtime and no platform library."
  NFR-002,"Shared: Legible Unavailability",legible-unavailability,"Every failed requirement, refused contribution or failed check names the primitive or requirement, the reason and a remedy the user can act on. Each report is structured so a test asserts its fields."
  NFR-003,"Shared: Fail Closed",fail-closed,"No sandbox is created with a partial set of contributions. A hook that fails, an environment that cannot be produced, a closure that cannot be derived, a requirement that is absent or a contribution the backend cannot apply fails create and leaves nothing behind. The only way to run without the devShell environment is to remove the step from the sequence."
  NFR-004,"Arch: Boundaries",boundaries,"The pure kind registry lives under `src/provision/kind/`, is reachable by configuration for settings validation, and is reachable by the resolver. Host preparation is a separate module reached only by the orchestrator. A backend imports neither. The boundaries are declared in `arch-lint.toml` and a violation fails the build."
  NFR-005,"Shared: No Values On Surfaces",no-values-on-surfaces,"No CLI output, MCP response, log line or persisted provenance carries an environment value. A test asserts that rendered provenance and inspection do not contain a fixture secret."
  NFR-006,"Shared: Test Selection",test-selection,"Parsing and contribution construction are unit-tested against recorded command output, with no nix and no network. Tests that need a real nix and a valid devShell are host tests, selected separately, and never build a derivation. Tests live in the module and are selectable by package and target."
  NFR-007,"Shared: Documentation",documentation,"The configuration reference documents the `devshell` step, its installable, the store view and the consent it needs. The doctor output is documented with the other preflight output, and `CONTEXT.md` plus the nix capability prompt carry the vocabulary."
  NFR-008,"Shared: Prototype Is Not Shipped",prototype-not-shipped,"The prototype stays under `adrs/2026-11-07-devshell-environment/poc/`, and no production module refers to it."
  NFR-009,"Shared: No New Supervisor",no-new-supervisor,"The host step runs nix as a child process and reads its output. It adds no daemon, no long-lived process and no background service."
acceptance[17]{id,title,slug,description}:
  AC-001,"Step: Environment Is The DevShell's",environment-is-direnv,"Against this repository's flake, the contributed environment contains the 18 exported-but-empty build-phase variables, the caller's RUSTFLAGS is absent, PATH still leads with the devShell's CARGO_HOME entry, and SSH_AUTH_SOCK, BITWARDEN_SSH_AUTH_SOCK, DOCKER_HOST, DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS and WAYLAND_DISPLAY are absent. HOME, PWD, OLDPWD, SHLVL and `_` are absent."
  AC-002,"Shared: Contributions At Step Position",contributions-at-position,"A recording backend receives the environment and mounts keyed to the devshell step's position: a command step before it sees the default environment, one after it sees the prepared environment, and a backend whose sequence does not name the step receives none of its contributions."
  AC-003,"Step: Closure Equals Query",closure-equals-query,"The mounts equal the de-duplicated output of `nix path-info -r` over the devShell's output path, one mount per path, and the count matches the query. With the whole store view, the mounts are the store root alone. The doctor reports the count and the view."
  AC-004,"Host: Unrealised Refused",unrealised-refused,"With the devShell not valid in the store, create fails as Unavailable naming the installable and `nix develop <installable>`, the doctor reports the same, and the store gains no output path for it. A host test observes only the derivation being written."
  AC-005,"Host: No Nix Refused",no-nix-refused,"With no nix on PATH, readiness and create fail as Unavailable naming the primitive and the remedy, and the doctor reports it without creating anything."
  AC-006,"Config: Consent Gate",consent-gate,"A devshell step in a project outside allowed-projects is refused as Denied naming the identity and both settings, and no nix process starts. The same project in allowed-projects prepares, and allow-project-setup permits every project."
  AC-007,"Core: Persistence Across Processes",persistence-across-processes,"A sandbox created with a devshell step reports the same environment and mounts to a second process's exec and inspect, and delete removes the contributions from the record."
  AC-008,"Core: No Shell State",no-shell-state-accepted,"A bash function defined in the devShell is not available to a command in the sandbox, no file is written to make it appear, and inspection says the sandbox carries no shell state."
  AC-009,"Core: No Socket Or Network Access",no-socket-or-network,"The request carries no daemon socket, no store write and no network access. Its read-only mounts are the closure members and the workspace, and a test asserts the mount set exactly."
  AC-010,"Config: Step Shape Refused",step-shape-refused,"A devshell step with an unknown key, an unknown kind or a missing installable fails at load naming the key or kind and the identity, and a second devshell step in one backend's sequence is refused naming both identities."
  AC-011,"CLI: Doctor Does Not Mutate",doctor-no-mutation,"Running the doctor on a project with a devshell step creates no sandbox, workspace or branch, and the store gains no path. A host test compares the store listing before and after."
  AC-012,"Shared: Provenance Carries No Value",provenance-no-value,"Inspection and MCP responses carry the step's identity, kind and changed variable names with change kinds, and no value. A fixture secret appears in no rendered output."
  AC-013,"Arch: Boundaries",boundaries,"The architecture lint denies a backend importing the provisioning or kind module, denies host preparation importing a backend, and a negative fixture fails the build."
  AC-014,"Shared: Contribution Refused",contribution-refused,"A step whose contribution the backend cannot apply is refused before anything is created, naming the contribution, the backend, the reason and the remedy. The backend is never called and the doctor reports the same."
  AC-015,"Arch: Registry Proven",registry-proven,"A test-only third kind registers without changing the contract or the backend. The backend receives its contributions and never its kind, and the contract compiles with no variant for it."
  AC-016,"Step: Empty Variables Kept",empty-variables-kept,"A `set -u` command that reads `patches` inside the sandbox succeeds, and the contributed environment contains `patches` with an empty value."
  AC-017,"Shared: Docker Rejects",docker-rejects,"With Docker selected and a devshell step in the sequence, create fails as Unsupported naming the backend, step and contribution before the container is created, and the doctor reports the same."
edgeCases[14]{id,title,slug,description}:
  EC-001,"Step: Hook Fails",hook-fails,"A shell hook that exits non-zero fails create as Failed, with the step identity and bounded output, and leaves no branch, workspace or compute. The doctor reports the same reason."
  EC-002,"Step: Hook Prints",hook-prints,"A shell hook that prints to stdout does not corrupt the environment, because records go to a file or a spare descriptor. A test with a banner-printing hook asserts every record is a well-formed assignment."
  EC-003,"Step: Not A DevShell",not-a-devshell,"An installable that evaluates but produces no devShell environment, such as a package rather than a shell, fails as Misconfigured naming the installable and what it produced."
  EC-004,"Host: Flakes Disabled",flakes-disabled,"With flakes disabled in the host's Nix configuration, readiness and create fail as Unavailable naming the experimental feature and the setting that enables it."
  EC-005,"Core: Backend Cannot Mount",backend-cannot-mount,"A backend that cannot mount the closure refuses with its own limit, the contribution, the reason and the remedy. The user can select the whole store view or a backend that can. No path is silently dropped."
  EC-006,"Core: Workspace Elsewhere",workspace-elsewhere,"When the workspace is presented at a path other than the project root, the recorded workspace-rooted values are rewritten and no store path is. A translation that would rewrite a store path is a defect and fails its test."
  EC-007,"Step: Shell Hook Execs A Shell",hook-execs-shell,"A shell hook or a caller's shell rc that execs another shell changes what the hook sees before it returns. The step takes the environment that is left when the hook exits and does not follow the exec. Recorded as a risk, not handled."
  EC-008,"Host: Dirty Tree",dirty-tree,"A dirty Git tree changes the flake source, so `print-dev-env` may write a source path to the store and the closure may differ from a clean checkout's. A create that fails after this leaves that store write behind, and the report does not claim otherwise."
  EC-009,"Shared: Docker Selected",docker-selected,"With a devshell step in the project and Docker selected, create fails as Unsupported naming the backend, step and contribution, and Docker is never called. The doctor reports the same."
  EC-010,"Step: DevShell Changed After Create",devshell-changed,"A sandbox created before the flake changed keeps the contributions it was created with. Creating again prepares them again and may differ, and inspection names the preparation's origin so the difference is visible."
  EC-011,"Shared: Command Needs Shell State",command-needs-shell-state,"A command that relies on a devShell bash function fails as it would in a plain shell, because no shell state is carried. The doctor says the sandbox carries none, and the remedy is a command that does not depend on it or a future contribution that adds it deliberately."
  EC-012,"Core: Closure Too Large",closure-too-large,"A closure larger than a backend's mount limit is refused by that backend with the limit, the contribution, the reason and the remedy. The whole store view or another backend may still work, and the doctor reports the limit."
  EC-013,"Config: Two DevShell Steps",two-devshell-steps,"Two devshell steps in one backend's sequence are Misconfigured, naming both identities, because one sandbox carries one prepared environment."
  EC-014,"Host: Nix Absent",nix-absent,"With no nix executable, the host requirement fails before any evaluation, and neither the doctor nor create writes a record or a store path."
